{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27273344","formula":"C₁₄H₁₅F₂N₃OS","hill":"C14H15F2N3OS","elements":["H","C","N","O","F","S"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"F":2.0,"H":15.0,"N":3.0,"O":1.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"Etamicastat"},"descriptions":{"en":"Etamicastat (INNTooltip International Nonproprietary Name; developmental code name BIA 5-453) is a peripherally selective dopamine β-hydroxylase (DBH) inhibitor which was under development for the treatment of hypertension (high blood pressure) and heart failure but was never marketed. The peripheral selectivity of etamicastat is in contrast to the earlier DBH inhibitor nepicastat, which is centrally active and produced associated side effects. Etamicastat was found to reduce blood pressure but not affect heart rate in clinical trials."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":10450387,"mass":311.35,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1[C@H](COC2=C1C=C(C=C2F)F)N3C(=CNC3=S)CCN","inchikey":"CWWWTTYMUOYSQA-LLVKDONJSA-N","iupac":"4-(2-aminoethyl)-3-[(3R)-6,8-difluoro-3,4-dihydro-2H-chromen-3-yl]-1H-imidazole-2-thione","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"10450387","atoms":36,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.309,"y":-3.389,"z":0.158,"el":"S"},{"x":3.799,"y":0.88,"z":2.302,"el":"F"},{"x":4.989,"y":0.238,"z":-2.229,"el":"F"},{"x":1.254,"y":0.199,"z":1.806,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.904,"y":-0.655,"z":0.044,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.658,"y":-2.046,"z":-0.189,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.495,"y":3.57,"z":-0.356,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.596,"y":-0.077,"z":0.221,"el":"C"},{"x":0.352,"y":-0.504,"z":-0.898,"el":"C"},{"x":0.015,"y":-0.474,"z":1.56,"el":"C"},{"x":1.767,"y":-0.129,"z":-0.559,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.071,"y":0.087,"z":-0.129,"el":"C"},{"x":2.135,"y":0.186,"z":0.756,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.258,"y":-2.035,"z":0.009,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.088,"y":1.57,"z":-0.147,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.107,"y":-0.755,"z":-0.